take the photo during 10-bit video from an 8-bit stream

classes com/oplus/ocs/camera/producer/mode/VideoMode getSurfaceFormatBySurfaceType() read
com.oplus.photo.10bit.format for the capture stream of a 10-bit video session. PhotoMode reads the same key
for its own 10-bit capture_yuv stream, so the 35 (YUV_420_888) set for video snapshots also turned Photo's
"10-bit color" stream into 8-bit YUV, which the 10-bit HEIF writer reads as P010: a green photo with the
image twice side by side. VideoMode now returns 35 for its capture stream without reading the key, and the
key is back at its default (34, P010) for Photo.

